Title: Fix dead grep and missing trap cleanup in test_ready.sh claimed tests
Created: 2026-05-04
Author: claude

--- log ---
2026-05-04T22:30Z claude created — two hygiene findings from PR #43 review

--- body ---
## Context

PR #43 review identified two minor hygiene issues in the new claimed-ticket
tests added to `tests/test_ready.sh`:

1. **Dead grep** (line ~379): `echo "$output" | grep '"id": "0098"' | grep -q '"claimed": true'`
   never fires because `"id"` and `"claimed"` are on separate lines in the
   multi-line JSON output. The `claimed_ok` flag is always set by the fallback
   `tr '\n' ' '` block below it. The dead path is confusing to read.

2. **Missing trap cleanup** for `test/0098-claim` branch: the branch is created
   mid-test but is only cleaned up on the happy path. If the test fails between
   creation (line ~375) and deletion (line ~403), the branch persists and will
   cause false `claimed=true` results in future test runs.

## Actions

1. Remove the dead `grep '"id": "0098"'` pipe (lines ~378-381 in test_ready.sh).
   The fallback logic (`tr '\n' ' '` + `grep -o '{[^}]*"id": "0098"[^}]*}'`)
   already handles multi-line JSON correctly; keep only that path.

2. Add `test/0098-claim` to the EXIT trap so it is always cleaned up:
   ```sh
   trap 'rm -rf "$FIXTURES/ready"; git branch -D test/0098-claim 2>/dev/null || true' EXIT
   ```
   Replace the existing trap at the top of the file (line ~14).

## Test

```sh
# After the fix, introduce a deliberate failure between branch create and delete:
# The branch must be gone after test exit regardless.
git branch test/0098-claim 2>/dev/null || true
sh tests/test_ready.sh || true
git branch --list test/0098-claim   # must be empty
```

Also verify the full test suite still passes: `make test`.

## Exit criteria

- Dead grep block removed; `claimed_ok` detection uses only the `tr`-based path
- `test/0098-claim` branch deleted by the EXIT trap even when tests fail mid-suite
- `make test` passes (all 129 tests)
